## Environment split

Browser-safe (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only):

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_PARTNER_ID`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ISSUER_DID`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ISSUE_PROGRAM_ID`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_VERIFY_PROGRAM_ID`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_ENV`

Issuer backend (`apps/backend/.env`, never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`):

- `NODE_ENV`
- `DATABASE_URL` (optional in sandbox)
- `ISSUER_ORIGIN`
- `PARTNER_ID`
- `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_KID`
- `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_ALG`
- `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_DER`
- `PARTNER_JWKS`
- `API_KEY`
- `ADMIN_API_KEY`

Web server-only (never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`):

- `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_KID`
- `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_DER`
- `PARTNER_JWKS`
- `AIR_VERIFY_PROGRAM_ID`, `AIR_TRUSTED_ISSUERS`, `AIR_EXPECTED_VCT`, `AIR_REQUIRED_CLAIMS` (verification)

## Anti-references

- Do not put `PARTNER_PRIVATE_KEY_DER`, `API_KEY`, or `ADMIN_API_KEY` in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Do not sign Partner JWTs in the browser
- Do not reuse one JWT across users or across issue + verify; issuance tokens carry `scope: "issue"`, verification tokens `scope: "verify"`
- Do not change the `ISSUER_ORIGIN` host after issuing
- Do not act on a browser-side `Compliant` result without backend verification
- Do not assume Testnet credentials exist on mainnet
- Do not skip JWKS because login already works
- Do not call Privy directly for agentic wallets
